{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>איש אל רעהו הבה</b> (Each man to his fellow — come) ס\"ת שלוה (the sedrah's notarikon: שלוה), because of the excessive שלוה that they had, they sinned:" "<b> לאבן</b> (for stone) — twice in the Masorah: here, and the other: וימת לבו בקרבו והוא היה לאבן (and his heart died within him and he became like a stone), regarding Nabal. Just as there it speaks of death, so too here death — for it was harder for them than death when a stone fell from the tower:"], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "ס\"ת = סוף טעם or סוד תורה; here the letters ש-ל-ה are extracted from the phrase as a notarikon acrostic."}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:15:57.740563376Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}